id: questions/open-questions
title: "What is still unresolved?"
kind: lacuna-index
status: preview
updated: 2026-09-13

purpose: >
  Keep unanswered, disputed, deferred, and decision-changing questions visible
  so the repository or observing agent does not manufacture closure.

template: templates/open-question.yawn

open_questions:
  - question: "Where do the sealed-question answer records persist (the answer and reason_match beats of core/articulation-floor.yawn), so that records/articulation-floor.yawn can be recomputed from more than one device?"
    coordinate: "runtime/articulation-answer-persistence"
    why_it_matters: "On 2026-09-13 every queued decision in records/yawn.bot-state.yawn and every axis in question-packets/polanyi.yawn carries a sealed prediction; the runtime reveals it after an answer and asks whether the sealed reason was the reason. Those answer records are what the floor is computed from, and today they live only on the answering device, so the public slice at https://yawn.bot/status shows n zero and a device-local floor beside it. This is the proposition-persistence question below, extended to a record with a schema (schemas/articulation-floor.v0.1.schema.json) and a validator; the same answer should settle both."
    evidence_needed:
      - the answer to runtime/proposition-persistence below
      - one round trip: an answer record written from the surface, read back by lib/articulation-floor-v0.1.mjs computeFloor, and shown on /status with its n
      - the authority flags under which a runtime may append to the answer ledger
    owner: Dave
    question_status: open
    blocks_action: false
    review_after: "before any floor is read as a verdict (ten closed records)"

  - question: "Which model may write the seal for a question that carries no attributed recommendation, and what re-ask gap and cap should the loop use?"
    coordinate: "runtime/seal-model-and-cadence"
    why_it_matters: "A decision's seal is its recommendation and needs no model; the Polanyi packet's seals were written by the agent from the records it cites. Any other question (a saved Yawn's inquiries, Dave's own open inquiries) has no prediction to seal without a provider call, which is a paid effect that needs Dave's authorization. core/articulation-floor.yawn states a 21-day re-ask gap and a one-in-five cap as defaults; both are tunable and neither has been chosen by Dave."
    evidence_needed:
      - which provider and version, under what approval boundary, may seal a prediction
      - the cadence Dave wants for re-asks, or confirmation of the defaults
      - a record of the first ten closed answers so the defaults can be judged against data
    owner: Dave
    question_status: open
    blocks_action: false
    review_after: "before the loop is extended past decisions and the Polanyi packet"

  - question: "Where does an answer given on yawn.bot/dave to an open decision persist: a bound orientation stream for that coordinate, a runtime table, or a proposal record in this repository, and under which authority flags?"
    coordinate: "runtime/proposition-persistence"
    why_it_matters: "On 2026-09-13 yawn.bot/dave began opening each ranked decision in place with its candidates and the chat composer; what Dave writes there is sorted to a proposition and kept on his device, and 'Continue in a Yawn' hands it to /new. The decision records here say a chosen candidate is his proposal until he fills choice:, but nothing says where that proposal lives between the device and the record. Until answered, the device thread and the /new handoff are the whole path, and a second device sees nothing."
    evidence_needed:
      - the orientation stream contract for a coordinate that is not a saved Yawn
      - a proposal event shape with authored_by and epistemic_status
      - one round trip from the surface to a record Dave can read back
    owner: Dave
    question_status: open
    blocks_action: false
    review_after: "before the proposition workspace is relied on across devices"

  - question: "Which git identity should commits made on Dave's behalf carry, now that Vercel refuses to build a commit whose author is not a member of the Yawn team?"
    coordinate: "runtime/commit-identity"
    why_it_matters: "On 2026-09-13 Vercel declined the preview build of yawn.bot commit b5c4fc6 because its author, the GitHub account daveforman, is not a member of the Yawn team on Vercel; the merge commits that main deploys from are authored by the yawn-ai account. CONTRIBUTING.md says the git identity is not attribution and asks for an Authored-By trailer instead, so the identity is free to be chosen for the pipeline: add daveforman to the Vercel team, or author agent commits under the yawn-ai identity with the trailer carrying who is answerable."
    evidence_needed:
      - Vercel team membership
      - a preview deployment that builds
    owner: Dave
    question_status: open
    blocks_action: false
    review_after: "before the next agent commit on yawn.bot that needs a preview deployment"

  - question: "When is yawn-ai/web-game archived, and which inbound links and integrations must move to yawn-ai/yawn.bot first?"
    coordinate: "runtime/repository-identity"
    why_it_matters: "Dave stated on 2026-09-12 that web-game is the older repository and is to be archived. Archiving is reversible on GitHub, but it breaks nothing only if every live pointer already names yawn.bot; the pointers in this repository were corrected the same day, the ones outside it are uninventoried."
    evidence_needed:
      - inbound link inventory
      - Vercel and GitHub integration inventory
      - archive receipt
    owner: Dave
    question_status: open
    blocks_action: false
    review_after: "before archiving the repository"

  - question: "Which exact .yawn protocol revision should govern the official YAWN.bot runtime?"
    coordinate: "runtime/protocol-pin"
    why_it_matters: "The runtime must not silently change behavior when the public protocol evolves."
    evidence_needed:
      - accepted public protocol commit
      - compatibility result against the runtime
    owner: Dave
    question_status: open
    blocks_action: true
    review_after: "before canonical production reconciliation"

  - question: "Which YAWN.bot contracts are public protocol and which remain private implementation?"
    coordinate: "public-private-boundary"
    why_it_matters: "The public repo should teach portable coherence without exposing private memory or proprietary implementation."
    evidence_needed:
      - secret and private-reference scan
      - public contract inventory
      - owner-reviewed promotion list
    owner: Dave
    question_status: open
    blocks_action: true
    review_after: "before public publication"

  - question: "What is the first production projection-equivalence receipt?"
    coordinate: "runtime/projection-proof"
    why_it_matters: "Wallet, phone, desktop, and world surfaces must share one orientation revision and authority state."
    evidence_needed:
      - authenticated runtime fixture
      - wallet and desktop screenshots
      - orientation revision comparison
      - console and runtime logs
    owner: YAWN.bot
    question_status: open
    blocks_action: true
    review_after: "before declaring production healthy"

recently_resolved:
  - question: "Should the official YAWN.bot GitHub repository slug change from web-game to yawn-bot?"
    answer: "Yes. The official YAWN.bot runtime is https://github.com/yawn-ai/yawn.bot with its Supabase database; https://github.com/yawn-ai/web-game is the older address, superseded and to be archived. Stated by Dave on 2026-09-12 and recorded on his behalf; provisional until he confirms it in a record he writes."
    question_status: answered-provisionally
    epistemic_status: reported
    owner: Dave
    answered_on: 2026-09-12
    proof_refs:
      - migrations/2026-09-12-cohere-vocabulary-and-attribution.yawn
      - yawn.yawn
      - agents/yawn.bot.yawn
    supersedes:
      - "Which codebase is the official YAWN.bot runtime? (2026-07-11 answer naming web-game)"
  - question: "Which codebase is the official YAWN.bot runtime?"
    answer: "The codebase at https://github.com/yawn-ai/web-game is the official YAWN.bot runtime."
    question_status: superseded
    superseded_on: 2026-09-12
    superseded_by: "the repository-slug answer above; the same codebase is now addressed at https://github.com/yawn-ai/yawn.bot"
    owner: Dave
    proof_refs:
      - records/yawn-bot-runtime-promotion-2026-07-11.yawn

states:
  - open
  - answered-with-evidence
  - answered-provisionally
  - disputed
  - deferred
  - superseded

rules:
  - "An unanswered question remains visible."
  - "A provisional answer is labeled provisional."
  - "Corrections supersede interpretations without erasing source history."
  - "Questions that do not change a decision need not block movement."

connects:
  lacuna: core/lacuna.yawn
  question_packets: question-packets/node.yawn
  feedback: feedback/form.yawn
  next_moves: records/next-move-ledger.yawn
  runtime_promotion: records/yawn-bot-runtime-promotion-2026-07-11.yawn
